    "title": "Final Project: Responsible AI Use Guide",
    "long_instructions": "Throughout this professional learning module, you explored the major ideas, instructional strategies, and student experiences that shape Thinking Critically About AI.\r\n\r\nThe Generate and Judge Guide helps students synthesize those experiences into a project that combines testing, evidence collection, reflection, judgment, and communication.\r\n\r\n## Project Rubric\r\n\r\nBelow is the project rubric students use throughout the unit. Notice how the rubric emphasizes reasoning, context, evidence, and conditional thinking rather than simply “getting the right answer.”\r\n\r\n<table style=\"width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; margin:25px 0px;\">\r\n  <tr style=\"background-color:#048899; color:#ffffff;\">\r\n    <th style=\"padding:10px; text-align:left; border:1px solid #cccccc; font-size:16px;\">Guide Section</th>\r\n    <th style=\"padding:10px; text-align:left; border:1px solid #cccccc; font-size:16px;\">4 - Exceeds</th>\r\n    <th style=\"padding:10px; text-align:left; border:1px solid #cccccc; font-size:16px;\">3 - Meets</th>\r\n    <th style=\"padding:10px; text-align:left; border:1px solid #cccccc; font-size:16px;\">2 - Approaching</th>\r\n    <th style=\"padding:10px; text-align:left; border:1px solid #cccccc; font-size:16px;\">1 - Beginning</th>\r\n  </tr>\r\n\r\n  <tr style=\"background-color:#F5F7F8;\">\r\n    <td style=\"padding:10px; border:1px solid #cccccc; font-size:16px;\"><strong>Understanding<br>What AI Is</strong></td>\r\n    <td style=\"padding:10px; border:1px solid #cccccc; font-size:16px;\">Predicts where AI will fail before it does, and adjusts approach based on the task</td>\r\n    <td style=\"padding:10px; border:1px solid #cccccc; font-size:16px;\">Can explain specific reasons AI fails and applies that to understanding real examples</td>\r\n    <td style=\"padding:10px; border:1px solid #cccccc; font-size:16px;\">Knows AI can be wrong, but treats errors as random. Repeats rules without understanding them</td>\r\n    <td style=\"padding:10px; border:1px solid #cccccc; font-size:16px;\">AI is either always right or always wrong, no in between</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"padding:10px; border:1px solid #cccccc; font-size:16px;\"><strong>Testing and<br>Evaluating AI</strong></td>\r\n    <td style=\"padding:10px; border:1px solid #cccccc; font-size:16px;\">Has a consistent evaluation process they can describe and reuse across different tasks and situations.</td>\r\n    <td style=\"padding:10px; border:1px solid #cccccc; font-size:16px;\">Tests prompts deliberately, checks claims against other sources, and explains what they found and why it matters.</td>\r\n    <td style=\"padding:10px; border:1px solid #cccccc; font-size:16px;\">Notices some prompts work better than others but cannot explain why one is more reliable.</td>\r\n    <td style=\"padding:10px; border:1px solid #cccccc; font-size:16px;\">Uses the first AI response as a final answer, or dismisses AI without engaging with it at all.</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n\r\n  <tr style=\"background-color:#F5F7F8;\">\r\n    <td style=\"padding:10px; border:1px solid #cccccc; font-size:16px;\"><strong>Risk and<br>Responsibility</strong></td>\r\n    <td style=\"padding:10px; border:1px solid #cccccc; font-size:16px;\">Recognizes that how careful to be depends on the context — stakes, audience, and task type — and can explain why.</td>\r\n    <td style=\"padding:10px; border:1px solid #cccccc; font-size:16px;\">Connects risk to specific consequences and makes deliberate choices based on what's at stake.</td>\r\n    <td style=\"padding:10px; border:1px solid #cccccc; font-size:16px;\">Knows basic safety rules but cannot explain the harm those rules are designed to prevent.</td>\r\n    <td style=\"padding:10px; border:1px solid #cccccc; font-size:16px;\">No awareness of what could go wrong when using or acting on AI output.</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"padding:10px; border:1px solid #cccccc; font-size:16px;\"><strong>Making Conditional<br>Judgments</strong></td>\r\n    <td style=\"padding:10px; border:1px solid #cccccc; font-size:16px;\">Offers multiple layered conditions for using AI and recognizes those conditions shift depending on the situation.</td>\r\n    <td style=\"padding:10px; border:1px solid #cccccc; font-size:16px;\">Completes \"AI can ___ as long as ___\" with a specific condition grounded in their own experience.</td>\r\n    <td style=\"padding:10px; border:1px solid #cccccc; font-size:16px;\">Attempts a condition, but it is too vague to be meaningful — e.g., \"as long as you're careful.\"</td>\r\n    <td style=\"padding:10px; border:1px solid #cccccc; font-size:16px;\">Views AI as simply good or bad with no conditions or context-sensitivity.</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"background-color:#F5F7F8; padding:20px; border-radius:10px; margin:30px 0px;\">\r\n\r\n<strong>Reflection:</strong> Which part of this project do you think would be most challenging for your students: testing AI systems, evaluating evidence, or making nuanced judgments about responsible AI use? Why?\r\n\r\n</div>",
